### Output formats

#### CSV
That format value is **csv** in the payload.
It's the recommended format for machine consumption.

**Example**
<pre>
day,advertiser_billable_volume,teads_billing-usd
2020-11-23T00:00:00Etc/GMT,30622,197.68621
</pre>

#### JSONV1 (JSON format)
That format value is **jsonv1** in the payload.

**Example**
<pre>
{
    "filters": {
        "placement": [
            17270
        ]
    },
    "dimensions": [
        "day",
        "placement"
    ],
    "metrics": [
        "placementCall",
        "start", "complete",
        "click", "impression",
        "firstQuartile",
        "midpoint",
        "thirdQuartile",
        "teads_billing-eur"
    ],
    "date": {
        "start": "2020/01/01 00:00:00 +00:00",
        "end": "2020/01/01 23:59:59 +00:00"
    },
    "lines": [
        [
            "2020/01/01",
            "17270 - Inread",
            "1 000",
            "99",
            "5",
            "2",
            "98",
            "100",
            "50",
            "20",
            "0.40000\\ EUR"
        ]
    ],
    "totals": [
        "1 000",
        "99",
        "5",
        "2",
        "100",
        "75",
        "50",
        "20",
        "0.40000\\ EUR"
    ]
}
</pre>

#### XLSX
That format value is **xlsx** in the payload.
You may omit it as it's the default output format.
XSLX is the Excel format. It's the most convenient output for customers that want to get an overview of their statistics. Teads manager users receive reports as XLSX files.

### Dimensions
#### **Publisher dimensions**
#### Publisher
- It's aggregating stats for all its websites or all its publishers in case of an adnetwork
<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
</table>

#### Website
- It's aggregating stats for all its placements

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>website</td><td>the id & the name of the website</td></tr>
<tr><td>website_domain</td><td>the domain of the website</td></tr>
</table>

#### Page
- A page is integrated on a publisher’s website as a new generic tag. it only embeds one information from Teads, the pageId.

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>page</td><td>the id & the name of the page</td></tr>
</table>

#### Placement
- it is a space in which are accessible data from all campaigns that are served on one specific script, on one or several pages from a website across one or several formats and environments

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>placement</td><td>the id & the name of the placement</td></tr>
</table>

#### Header bidding

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>hb_provider</td><td>Provider of the the Header Bidding implementation. null or N/A means the integration is not Header Bidding.</td></tr>
</table>

#### **Programmatic dimensions**
#### Adsource
- it is the "parent" of a connection, it's usually a DSP, VAST Compliant or the marketplace

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>adsource</td><td>the id & the name of the ad source</td></tr>
</table>

#### Connection
- it is a specific adsource configuration for an entity using SSP

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>connection</td><td>the id & the name of the connection</td></tr>
<tr><td>connection_type</td><td>it could be a rtb or fixed</td></tr>
<tr><td>connection_is_moat</td><td>if moat is activated or not on the connection level</td></tr>
</table>

#### Scenario
- it is a set of connection configurations to broadcast. Scenario is only usable for SSP stats.

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>scenario_id</td><td>the id of the scenario</td></tr>
<tr><td>scenario_name</td><td>the name of the scenario</td></tr>
</table>

#### **Campaign dimensions**
#### Advertiser
- it is the brand for which the ad is advertising ex Coca, BMW or Mercedes.

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>advertiser</td><td>the id & the name of the advertiser</td></tr>
<tr><td>advertiser_name</td><td>the name of the advertiser</td></tr>
<tr><td>advertiser_domain</td><td>domain name of the advertiser</td></tr>
</table>

#### Agency
- it is the agency responsible for an ad or a connection example Group M, Havas or Videology.

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>agency</td><td>the id & the name of the agency</td></tr>
<tr><td>agency_name</td><td>the name of the agency</td></tr>
</table>

#### Ad
- it is aggregating stats for all its insertions

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>ad</td><td>the id & the name of the ad</td></tr>
<tr><td>ad_type</td><td>the type of the ad as defined in database, either managed, monitoring or agency</td></tr>
<tr><td>ad_is_moat</td><td>if moat is activated or not on the ad level</td></tr>
<tr><td>ad_is_test</td><td>if test is activated or not on the ad level</td></tr>
</table>

#### Insertion
- it is a sub-division of a campaign with specific criteria (volume, targeting,capping, format etc…)

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion</td><td>the id & the name of the insertion</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_type</td><td>the type of the insertion, it can be either direct sold, intragroup or a self serve</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_budget</td><td>the budget of the insertion as a number (no currency)</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_start_date</td><td>the start date of the insertion</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_end_date</td><td>the end date of the insertion</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_volume_value</td><td>If a volume is defined on the insertion, this dimension prints the volume limit count ex volume at 60000 start prints "60000"</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_volume_event</td><td>If a volume is defined on the insertion, this dimension prints the volume limit count ex volume at 60000 start prints "start"</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_price_publisher</td><td>it is the buying price set up on the insertion level</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_price_publisher_cpm</td><td>if a price is defined on the insertion, the buying price value is displayed as a cost per mille</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_price_publisher_currency</td><td>If a price is defined on the insertion, this dimension prints the buying price currency ex price at 0.003$ on complete prints "USD"</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_price_advertiser</td><td>it is the selling price set up on the insertion level</td></tr>
<tr><td>insertion_price_advertiser_event</td><td>If a selling price is defined on the insertion, this dimension prints the selling price event ex price at 0.003$ on complete prints "complete"</td></tr>
</table>

#### Creative
- it is a media element that corresponds to the ad.

<table><tr><td>Reporting dimension</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>creative</td><td>the id & the name of the creative</td></tr>
</table>

