### Metrics
Metrics data are updated around every 30 minutes.

#### Publisher integration metrics

<table>
<tr><td>Reporting metric</td><td>Logged events</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>placementCall</td><td>callJS + placementCall</td><td>Records that the script has been called by each placement of the webpage or app. This metric will replace callJS as a more descriptive metric.</td></tr>
<tr><td>placementCapping</td><td>placementCapping</td><td>The placement capping has been reached.</td></tr>
<tr><td>slot_available</td><td>slot_available + slotAvailable</td><td>The browser and device are compatible and a slot is available on the webpage. Will be phased out and replaced by slotAvailable)</td></tr>
<tr><td>slotAvailable</td><td>slot_available + slotAvailable</td><td>The browser and device are compatible and a slot is available on the webpage (previously slot_available)</td></tr>
<tr><td>adAvailable-success</td><td>adAvailable-success</td><td>The SSP responded with a compatible ad to serve</td></tr>
<tr><td>adCall</td><td>adCall</td><td>An ad is called because the user has scrolled to the slot</td></tr>
<tr><td>adNotAvailable-ivt-tag</td><td>adNotAvailable-ivt-tag</td><td>Our 3rd party partner TAG has declared the current session as invalid</td></tr>
<tr><td>adNotAvailable-blockedSite-doubleVerify</td><td>adNotAvailable-blockedSite-doubleVerify</td><td>Our 3rd party partner DV has blacklisted this website</td></tr>
<tr><td>adNotAvailable-ivt-doubleVerify</td><td>adNotAvailable-ivt-doubleVerify</td><td>Our 3rd party partner TAG has declared the current session as invalid</td></tr>
<tr><td>integration-rate</td><td>slot_available / placementCall</td><td>Represents the efficiency of our script in finding a slot on your publishers' pages</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot</td><td>noSlot + noSlot-selector + noSlot-filter + noSlot-avoid +noSlot-size + noSlot-BTF + noSlot-minimum + noSlot-minimumBelow + noSlot-content + noSlot-position</td><td>The slot defined could not be found on the page. it's the sum of the noSlot events. You may use noSlot-details to get the distribution. noSlot behavior on the legacy engine is the one from noSlot-details.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-avoid</td><td>noSlot-avoid</td><td>There is a match to the avoidSlot defined in the script.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-BTF</td><td>noSlot-BTF</td><td>The format could not find a slot below the fold.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-content</td><td>noSlot-content</td><td>The format detects that the number of characters on the page is too low or it contains forbidden DOM elements (as defined in the format)</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-details</td><td>Display 9 columns with the following metrics: noSlot-selector, noSlot-filter, noSlot-avoid, noSlot-size, noSlot-BTF, noSlot-minimum, noSlot-minimumBelow, noSlot-content, noSlot-position</td><td>Defines slot errors based on the webpage structure (DOM). Selecting this metric in your report dimensions will display all noSlot-x metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-DOM</td><td>noSlot-DOM</td><td>Will be phased out in phased out in favour of noSlot-selector</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-filter</td><td>noSlot-filter</td><td>There is a match to the filterdefined in the script.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-minimum</td><td>noSlot-minimum + noSlot-MinSlot</td><td>There is no slot available below the minSlot defined in the script. noSlot-MinSlot will be phased out.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-MinSlot</td><td>noSlot-MinSlot</td><td>Will be phased out in phased out in favour of noSlot-minimum</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-position</td><td>noSlot-position</td><td>the format detects if the top position of the slot meets the minimum format requirements and checks that the format will not distort the general page layout</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-selector</td><td>noSlot-selector + noSlot-DOM</td><td>The slot defined could not be found on the page. noSlot-DOM will be phased out and replaced by noSlot-selector.</td></tr>
<tr><td>noSlot-size</td><td>noSlot-size</td><td>The format could not find a slot with acceptable size dimensions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>passback</td><td> </td><td>Will be phased out in favour of passback-noAd or passback-integration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>passback-noAd</td><td> </td><td>A noAd event has occurred and the publisher has defined a fallback in the placement settings</td></tr>
</table>

