#### Programmatic metrics

<table>
<tr><td>Reporting metric</td><td>Logged events</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>ssp_auction</td><td>ssp_auction</td><td>Number of auctions triggered (only available for placements)</td></tr>
<tr><td>ssp_bidrequest</td><td>ssp_bidrequest</td><td>Number of bid requests we made to the DSP</td></tr>
<tr><td>dsp_response_bid</td><td>dsp_response_bid</td><td>Number of valid bid from the DSP</td></tr>
<tr><td>dsp_response_error</td><td>dsp_response_error</td><td>Number of bid responses which resulted in an error (unable to get a bid)</td></tr>
<tr><td>dsp_response_filtered</td><td>dsp_response_filtered</td><td>Number of bid responses which resulted in a filtering (invalid bid)</td></tr>
<tr><td>dsp_response_declined</td><td>dsp_response_declined</td><td>Number of bids that were declined by the DSP (the DSP isn't interested by the deal)</td></tr>
<tr><td>ssp_timeout</td><td>ssp_timeout</td><td>Number of timeouts on ssp_bidrequest, i.e. it took too long for the DSP to answer to the bid request</td></tr>
<tr><td>ssp_auctionwon</td><td>ssp_auctionwon</td><td>Number of won auctions</td></tr>
<tr><td>dsp_response-rate</td><td>dsp_response_bid / ssp_bidrequest</td><td>Represents the ratio of bid response we receive from a dsp over the number of bidrequests we send</td></tr>
<tr><td>ssp_win-rate</td><td>ssp_auctionwon / ssp_bidrequest</td><td>Represents the ratio of auction won by a dsp over the number of bidrequests we send to him</td></tr>
</table>

#### Finance metrics

<table>
<tr><td>Logged events</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>teads_billing</td><td>Teads billing is the amount paid by Teads to a publisher. Practically, it contains all the money Teads owe the publisher regardless of if it's part of the margin activity or collect & fee activity.</td></tr>
<tr><td>income</td><td>Income is the amount of money that a publisher generates through Teads platform. Practically, income = teads_billing + self served direct sold. If the publisher is a managed service income = teads_billing.</td></tr>
</table>

There are 3 ways of getting finance metrics:

##### Currency dimension with value metric

This method allows you to fetch currency as dimension and the metric value in its own column.

Example:

<table>
<tr><td>income_currency</td><td>income_value</td></tr>
<tr><td>EUR</td><td>0.1234</td></tr>
<tr><td>USD</td><td>0.5678</td></tr>
</table>

##### Converted metrics

This method allows you to have the sum of all currencies in a single column converted in the selected currency.

Example:

<table>
<tr><td>income_converted_usd</td></tr>
<tr><td>1.234</td></tr>
<tr><td>5.678</td></tr>
</table>

##### Expanded metrics (Deprecated)

income, along with all currency based finance metrics, is dynamic, meaning that you may get multiple metrics as the result.
Some publishers/adnetworks are working with Teads with multiple currencies and therefore might be billed in several currencies.
So that depending on the report they are doing, they might get different results. Currency codes used are based on ISO 4217.

These metrics are designed to work, with "income" as an example, as follows:
- The account doesn't have any income, we return "income" metric with "0"
- The account has only USD currency on income, we return a single metric as "income-usd"
- The account has 2 or more currencies on income, we return multiple columns like "income-usd", "income-eur" and "income-gbp"

Expanded metrics "teads_billing" and "income" will be deprecated starting January 1, 2024.
Starting January 1, 2024, expanded metrics will not return one column per currency in use, but one column for each of the 37 currencies that are supported by Teads, regardless of their usage.
We recommend to use one of the two other finance metrics methods above (Currency dimensions with Value metric or Converted metrics)

##### Specific currency metrics

You can request a currency specific income part by directly requesting it such as "income-usd".
However if multiple currencies are involved and you would like to get all revenues in a single currency, you can request the converted version "income_converted_usd" (which won't expand).

##### billable metrics

<table>
<tr><td>Logged events</td><td>Definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>publisher_billable_volume</td><td>Amount of events that require payment to the publisher</td></tr>
<tr><td>advertiser_billable_volume</td><td>Amount of events that require payment from the advertiser</td></tr>
</table>


